@td_psl_accounting
title: PSL presents the accumulated account
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
let ratchet =
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.45 +
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.24 +
    Math.max(0, 45 - (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0)) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0)) * 0.18;
if (Q.coalition_break_threat) ratchet += 10;
if (Q.abortion_cabinet_deadline) ratchet += 7;
if (Q.third_way_response == "PSL recognised as the coalition hinge") {
    ratchet += 8;
}
if (Q.third_way_response == "Equal bilateral agreements") {
    ratchet -= 4;
}
Q.psl_ratchet_score = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(ratchet))
);
Q.news_headline =
    "PSL converts the end of Third Way into a list of coalition terms";
!}

= The price was accumulated, not invented today

PSL's leverage is **[+ psl_ratchet_score +]/100**. It comes from farm protests,
the abortion roll call, the presidential result, its relationship with Lewica
and the cabinet's own dissent. The Left's opening line—**[+
third_way_response +]**—changes the negotiation, but does not erase that
history.

[? if coalition_break_threat: PSL's negotiators quote the earlier threat to
leave government as proof that every progressive vote now carries a cabinet
price.?]
[? if abortion_cabinet_deadline: The spring abortion deadline remains live.
PSL will not sign language that turns its free vote into automatic expulsion.?]
[? if psl_relation >= 55: The bilateral relationship is good enough for a
written trade; PSL does not need to manufacture a public humiliation.?]
[? if psl_relation < 35: Private channels are weak. Every demand is therefore
also a press conference and an invitation for the right to bid.?]

- @td_protocol
- @td_hold_line
- @td_roll_calls

@td_protocol
title: Sign a rural-social protocol without granting another rights veto
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity in government, otherwise 1 resource.
choose-if: (left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 1) or (left_in_government = 0 and resources >= 1)
unavailable-subtitle: No material offer can be attached to the protocol.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.left_in_government) Q.budget -= 1;
else Q.resources -= 1;
Q.psl_protocol_2025 =
    "Rural services and farm bargaining; no new social-policy veto";
Q.psl_relation += 6;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 5;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 3;
Q.rural_support += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.psl_ratchet_score = Math.max(0, Q.psl_ratchet_score - 10);
Q.news_headline =
    "A material PSL agreement draws a line around its conservative veto";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

